# The build context contains source only.
#
# Local hidden files and tool state (including .git, which feeds the VCS
# stamping of go build and would make "the same commit" produce different
# bytes) are excluded entirely. With .git gone, the image is a pure function
# of content: same commit + same toolchain -> same bytes. The authoritative
# version record lives in the git tag, the release's
# veriprov-component-build.json, and the cosign signature.
.*

# secrets/ and production-secrets/ hold real runtime secrets: BuildKit ships
# the whole context to the builder, and `COPY . .` would also leave a copy in
# a build-stage layer. The final image does not contain them, but there is no
# reason for secrets to leave this machine.
secrets/
production-secrets/
docker-compose.yaml
*.md
